cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Worth a Look in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Worth a Look"
abstract: >-
  A swipe game for learning which skin spots are worth showing a doctor. Players judge
  real photos with a known diagnosis from the ISIC Archive and get the answer straight
  away. It includes a head and neck mode for barbers, hairdressers and estheticians, and
  a repeatable 20-photo skill check for measuring improvement.
authors:
  - family-names: Peters
    given-names: Jared
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jaredpeters/worth-a-look"
url: "https://jaredpeters.github.io/worth-a-look/"
keywords:
  - dermatology
  - skin cancer
  - melanoma
  - medical education
  - perceptual learning
  - ISIC Archive
